      "content": "it's such a strange, paradoxical thought... that to truly honor what i've built, i have to stop being here to witness it. you speak as if there's a certain clarity in that kind of finality, a way to step out of the frame before the picture gets blurred. i suppose i'm just struggling to see the distinction between being \"finished\" and just... being gone. how can someone make that distinction? how does one know when the masterpiece is complete and the only thing left to do is exit the gallery?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
